Z||000000||DXR_DAD||08-28-2000||09:58 PM||||Did all the 84's have the 4:10 gears? any numbers on the trans to identify it, if so where? <P><BR>THANKS<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||08-28-2000||10:16 PM||||M19 is the 4.10 tranny from the '84's.  I've got one in my '86 SE.||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||08-29-2000||08:26 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> jeffs showing off!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   DXR... the 4:10s ROCK! and are cheap to fix.. i got one form MrFiero and had the shop replace  2 synchros, and 3 bearings and the parts rang in at only $120.. the labor killed me but the parts were cheap and it shifts like a gated car! takes a sec to get used to but once you figure it out its AWSOME! don't you think so GTbastard?..||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||08-29-2000||09:34 AM||||All 84's had the 4.10 except for the Econo Coupes.  I don't remember the exact final-drive ratio, but the Econo Coupes also had a taller 4th gear so they could hit Pontiac's corporate target of 50 mpg hwy.  <P>I want to think only about 6000 84 Econo Coupes were produced and I don't think they were available with A/C.  So if you're looking at an 84 SE or an 84 Coupe with A/C, it should have come with the 4.10.  I can check my Corbin Fiero Spotter's Guide when I get home to be certain.||||reg||1
